# Leeway binding for this repo

Generated {{DATE}} by leeway-sdlc {{VERSION}}. Read before any Leeway call. Never synced by
`sync-repo`: it is this repo's own.

server: {{SERVER_URL}}
product: {{PRODUCT_KEY}}
cli: {{CLI_COMMAND}}
friction-collector: {{FRICTION_COLLECTOR}}
filing-work: {{FILING_WORK}}

`cli:` is the command every skill runs in place of `leeway`: `leeway` when it is on the PATH, else a
path such as `node /path/to/leeway.js`. No credential belongs in this file or anywhere else in the
repo: `leeway login` keeps the sign-in on the machine.

`friction-collector:` is the issue of type `chore` that friction is filed under, as a ref such as
`{{PRODUCT_KEY}}-12`, or `n/a` and why. It is the product's, not a project's.

`filing-work:` is `plan-work` when filing work in Leeway counts as planning, so the managed block tells the
agent to invoke `plan-work` for it even while pairing, or `manual` when `plan-work` stays an opt-in;
`sync-repo` asks for it when this line is absent.

